namespace Stacks.RingedSpace

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099F] on the small Zariski site of a ringed space.** For a sheaf of ideals
`ℐ ⊆ 𝒪_X` of finite type the inclusion `D_comp(𝒪_X, ℐ) ⥤ D(𝒪_X)` has a left adjoint, so the
derived completion functor `(-)^∧` along `ℐ` exists.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete` at
`Stacks.RingedSpace.toRingedSite X`, restated because instance search does not find that
instance at a ringed site of this shape — the same restatement that
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_toRingedSite` of
`PushforwardCompletionTopos.lean` makes for the site presenting a ringed topos. -/
instance isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType
    (X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u})
    (I : _root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (toRingedSite X).O))))
    [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType] :
    (ObjectProperty.ι (RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u}
      (toRingedSite X) I)).IsRightAdjoint :=
  RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete (toRingedSite X) I

/-- **At a morphism between the small Zariski sites of two ringed spaces, `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` is of
finite type when `ℐ` is.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_inverseImageIdealSheaf` at
`Stacks.RingedSpace.toRingedSite`, restated for the same reason as
`isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType`: instance search does not find
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_inverseImageIdealSheaf_of_instance` at a ringed site
of this shape. Together with that instance it makes the derived completion functor along
`f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` available, by [Stacks, Tag 099F]. -/
instance isFiniteType_inverseImageIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType
    {X Y : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u}}
    (f : RingedSite.Hom (toRingedSite X) (toRingedSite Y))
    (I : _root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (toRingedSite Y).O))))
    [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType] :
    (RingedSite.inverseImageIdealSheaf.{u} f I).toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType :=
  RingedSite.isFiniteType_inverseImageIdealSheaf_of_instance.{u} f I

/-- **At a ringed space, a sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many global sections is of
finite type.** The small Zariski site has binary products — the intersection of two open sets —
so `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFiniteType_generatedIdealSheaf` applies: the generators,
which are sections over every open set at once, are in particular local generators over the
trivial covering of `⊤` by every open set.

This is what makes the statements of this file contain those of
`PushforwardCommutesCompletionGenerated.lean` rather than merely sit beside them. -/
instance isFiniteType_generatedIdealSheaf {X : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u}} {r : ℕ}
    (g : Fin r → CategoryTheory.Presheaf.globalSections
      ((toRingedSite X).O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})) :
    (RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf g).toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType :=
  RingedSite.isFiniteType_generatedIdealSheaf g

section Display

variable {X Y : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.{u, u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
  (I : _root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (toRingedSite Y).O))))
  (I' : _root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (toRingedSite X).O))))
  (hI : RingedSite.PushforwardIdealCompatible (toRingedSiteHom f) I I')

include hI in
/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0A0I], the left hand side of the display, at a morphism of ringed spaces and
sheaves of ideals of finite type.** `Rf_*(ℱ^∧)` is derived complete along `ℐ`, for an arbitrary
`ℱ ∈ D(𝒪_X)`, the completion on `X` being taken along any sheaf of ideals `ℐ'` of finite type
receiving `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ)` — in particular along the display's own `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X`.

The derived completion functor on `D(𝒪_X)` is produced from the finite-type hypothesis, by
`Stacks.RingedSpace.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 099F] — the step the source takes before writing the display down. The statement
itself is then [Stacks, Tag 099J]:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedCompletion` read at
the small Zariski sites of `X` and `Y`. -/
@[stacks 0A0I "the left hand side `Rf_*(ℱ^∧)` of Equation 52.7.0.1 is derived complete along \
`ℐ`, for an **arbitrary** object, at a morphism of ringed *spaces* read on its small Zariski \
sites, at the source's own data: a sheaf of ideals `ℐ` of finite type, the completion on `X` \
being taken along a sheaf of ideals `ℐ'` of finite type receiving `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ)`, as the \
display's `f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` does. The derived completion functor is produced from the finite-type \
hypothesis by [Stacks, Tag 099F], so it is an output here and not an input. Quasi-coherence of \
`ℐ` and of `ℱ` is not needed"]
theorem isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedCompletion_of_isFiniteType
    [I'.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    (K : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (toRingedSite X).O)))) :
    RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (toRingedSite Y) I
      ((@derivedPushforward.{u} _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (toRingedSiteHom f).toRingedToposSiteHom (_) (_)).obj
        ((RingedSite.derivedCompletion (toRingedSite X) I').obj K)) :=
  RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedCompletion
    (toRingedSiteHom f) I I' hI K

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0A0I] at a morphism of ringed spaces and sheaves of ideals of finite type,
for a derived-complete object.** The comparison `(Rf_*ℱ)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(ℱ^∧)` is invertible for every
`ℱ ∈ D(𝒪_X)` derived complete along `ℐ'`, where `ℐ ⊆ 𝒪_Y` and `ℐ' ⊆ 𝒪_X` are sheaves of ideals
of finite type with `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ) ⊆ ℐ'`.

Both derived completion functors are produced from the finite-type hypotheses by
[Stacks, Tag 099F], `Stacks.RingedSpace.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isFiniteType`, so
the data this statement takes is the source's own; quasi-coherence of `ℐ` and of `ℱ` is not
needed. The underlying statement is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_of_isDerivedComplete`
read at the small Zariski sites.

The restriction to a derived-complete `ℱ` is on the object: the invertibility for an arbitrary
`ℱ` is the assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0A0G], and it is proved — at a morphism of ringed *sites*
and at the constructed `ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` rather than at an independent parameter `ℐ'` — by
`RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_inverseImageIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`,
and at a morphism of schemes and a quasi-coherent `ℐ` of finite type by
`Scheme.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_idealSheafData_inverseImageIdealSheaf`. -/
@[stacks 0A0I "Equation 52.7.0.1 at a morphism of ringed *spaces* read on its small Zariski \
sites, for a **derived-complete** object, at the source's own data: two sheaves of ideals of \
finite type, `ℐ ⊆ 𝒪_Y` and `ℐ' ⊆ 𝒪_X` with `f^♯(f^{-1}ℐ) ⊆ ℐ'`, as the display's pair \
`ℐ, f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X` is. Both derived completion functors are produced from those finite-type \
hypotheses by [Stacks, Tag 099F], so no part of that tag is an input, and quasi-coherence of \
`ℐ` and of `ℱ` is not needed. The display for an arbitrary object is the invertibility half of \
[Stacks, Tag 0A0G]"]
theorem isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_of_isFiniteType_of_isDerivedComplete
    [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType] [I'.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    {K : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (toRingedSite X).O)))}
    (hK : RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (toRingedSite X) I' K) :
    IsIso ((RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison
      (toRingedSiteHom f) I I' hI).app K) :=
  RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_of_isDerivedComplete
    (toRingedSiteHom f) I I' hI hK

